	•	Section 2 Comments/Quotes: Table 1 states there were 71 subjects total, with 41 BOS and 30 non-BOS, and the text reports 53 men and 18 women with mean age 57 years. Female sex is therefore 18/71 = 25.4%. Race/ethnicity was not reported. Clinical background was reported through pretransplant diagnoses including idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis, COPD, cystic fibrosis, alpha-1-antitrypsin deficiency, and other.  ￼

Section 3: Intervention & AI Methods
	•	Primary ML Component: Yes
	•	Study Design: Retrospective Cohort
	•	AI Model Architecture: SVM
	•	Algorithm Name: Support vector machine with radial basis function kernel
	•	Input Variables (Data Modality): Imaging
	•	Comparator / Standard of Care: Other
	•	Validation Method: Other
	•	Explainability / Interpretability Used: No
	•	Feature Selection Method: Automated
	•	Hyperparameter Tuning Reported: No
	•	Section 3 Comments/Quotes: The article explicitly says the scans were analyzed retrospectively and that “supervised ML with support vector machines (SVMs) was used.” The model used significant qCT features derived from Student t tests, and a “radial basis functional kernel with default tuning parameters was used.” Inputs were qCT/FRI imaging features from paired inspiratory-expiratory CT scans. The main comparator was not another clinical model but rather baseline clinical/PFT variables, which the paper states could not significantly distinguish BOS from non-BOS at baseline. Validation used repeated random train-test partitions (90/10 for 1D and 2D, 80/20 for 3D), so “Other” is the most exact category.  ￼  ￼

